      "description": "Department of Family Medicine - Open Rank (JPF02261) - AP Recruit Skip to main content Recruit Home Open Recruitments Department of Family Medicine - Open Rank (JPF02261) Department of Family Medicine - Open Rank Apply now to Department of Family Medicine - Open Rank Job #JPF02261 Dept. of Family Medicine / School of Medicine / UC Riverside Position overview Position titles: Health Sciences Assistant Clinical Professor Health Sciences Associate Clinical Professor Health Sciences Clinical Professor Assistant Professor of Clinical X Associate Professor of Clinical X Professor of Clinical X Salary range: The posted UC salary scales ( Academic salaries | UCOP ) set the minimum pay determined by rank and step at appointment. The Base Salary range for this position is $131,200 - $344,400. This position includes membership in the health sciences compensation plan ( 2021 02 11 Hscp%20 Plan ), which provides eligibility for additional compensation. Application Window Open date: June 2, 2026 Most recent review date: Wednesday, Aug 5, 2026 at 11:59pm (Pacific Time) Applications received after this date will be reviewed by the search committee if the position has not yet been filled. Final date: Wednesday, Jun 30, 2027 at 11:59pm (Pacific Time) Applications will continue to be accepted until this date, but those received after the review date will only be considered if the position has not yet been filled. Position description The UCR Department of Family Medicine seeks full-time board-certified family physicians with a full and unrestricted California medical license to join a team of committed faculty who provide ambulatory and inpatient services within Riverside and San Bernardino Counties. Responsibilities of this position include clinical care, teaching medical students and residents as well as engaging in community-based participatory research, public service, quality initiatives and service to the University. Time will be provided to pursue scholarly activities and ensure academic promotion. The University of California, Riverside (UCR) is a world-class research university with an exceptionally diverse undergraduate student body. Its mission is explicitly linked to providing routes to educational success for underrepresented and first-generation college students. The successful applicant must qualify for an academic appointment in Professor of Clinical X or Health Sciences Clinical Professor series at the Assistant, Associate, or Full professor rank. Academic rank will be determined based on qualifications and experience with advancement through a series of structured, merit-based evaluations, occurring every 2-3 years, each of which includes substantial peer input. Basic qualifications M.D. or D.O. degree Hold a full and unrestricted license from the Medical Board of California Board Certified by the American Board of Family Medicine or American Board of Osteopathic Medicine Qualify for medical staff privileges at UCR Health and at UCR affiliated health settings Additional qualifications Demonstrated experience in teaching residents and medical students Preferred qualifications Commitment to UCR School of Medicine Mission Mission, Vision, Diversity, & Values Statements | School of Medicine Current practice with under-resourced and underinsured patients ranging from newborn to geriatrics and ambulatory low-risk prenatal care Acute Care Hospital Experience Fellowship in Addiction Medicine Fellowship in Community Medicine Fellowship in Geriatric Medicine Fellowship in Sports Medicine Fellowship in Street Medicine The posted UC salary scales ( Academic salaries | UCOP ) set the minimum pay determined by rank and step at appointment. See Table 5 for the salary range. The Base Salary range for this position is $131,200 - $344,400. This position includes membership in the health sciences compensation plan ( 2021 02 11 Hscp%20 Plan ), which provides eligibility for additional compensation. HS Clinical Professor: Apm 