    "https://aprecruit.ucr.edu/JPF02263": {
      "title": "Recruit",
      "description": "Department of Psychiatry and Neuroscience - Open Rank (JPF02263) - AP Recruit Skip to main content Recruit Home Open Recruitments Department of Psychiatry and Neuroscience - Open Rank (JPF02263) Department of Psychiatry and Neuroscience - Open Rank Apply now to Department of Psychiatry and Neuroscience - Open Rank Job #JPF02263 SOM Neuroscience / School of Medicine / UC Riverside Position overview Position titles: Health Sciences Assistant Clinical Professor Health Sciences Associate Clinical Professor Health Sciences Clinical Professor Assistant Professor of Clinical X Associate Professor of Clinical X Professor of Clinical X Assistant Adjunct Professor Associate Adjunct Professor Adjunct Professor Assistant Professor in Residence Associate Professor in Residence Professor in Residence Salary range: The posted UC salary scales ( Academic salaries | UCOP ) set the minimum pay determined by rank and step at appointment. The Base Salary range for this position is $131,200 - $344,400. This position includes membership in the health sciences compensation plan. ( 2021 02 11 Hscp%20 Plan ), which provides for eligibility for additional compensation. Application Window Open date: June 3, 2026 Most recent review date: Wednesday, Aug 5, 2026 at 11:59pm (Pacific Time) Applications received after this date will be reviewed by the search committee if the position has not yet been filled. Final date: Wednesday, Jun 30, 2027 at 11:59pm (Pacific Time) Applications will continue to be accepted until this date, but those received after the review date will only be considered if the position has not yet been filled. Position description The Division of Clinical Sciences at the University of California, Riverside School of Medicine (UCR SOM) invites applications for faculty positions in the Department of Psychiatry and Neurosciences. We are seeking outstanding clinical educators and clinician-scholars to join our growing academic department and participate in part-time and/or full-time inpatient and outpatient psychiatric practice within an academic medical center environment. UCR Psychiatry offers a collaborative and mission-driven environment in which faculty practice clinically while working alongside medical students, residents, fellows, and interdisciplinary trainees. Faculty are encouraged and supported in pursuing scholarly, educational, and community-engaged activities. Our department is actively engaged in translational and community-partnered research, with collaborations across the university and with regional healthcare systems. We welcome applicants with expertise across the full spectrum of psychiatric practice. Individuals with additional fellowship training or board certification in child and adolescent psychiatry, geriatric psychiatry, addiction psychiatry, forensic psychiatry, or consultation-liaison psychiatry are particularly encouraged to apply. A limited number of Medical Director roles (inpatient or outpatient) may also be available for qualified applicants with demonstrated leadership experience, including at least five years of clinical experience or a minimum of three years of administrative or program leadership in clinical settings. We also welcome applicants with clinical, research, or programmatic interests in areas such as: • LGBTQ+ mental health • Women’s mental health and reproductive psychiatry • Trauma-related disorders and PTSD • Health equity and health disparities • Community psychiatry and population mental health • Health services research • Neuropsychiatry • Developmental disorders and neurodiversity Experience or interest in telepsychiatry and innovative models of care delivery is desirable. Spanish language proficiency is highly valued given the needs of the communities we serve. UCR School of Medicine is a Hispanic-Serving Institution (HSI) and Minority-Serving Institution (MSI) located in one of the most diverse regions in the United States. Our mission includes expanding access to medical education and improving health outcomes in historically underserved communities. We welcome applicants who have demonstrated experience working with diverse populations and who are committed to advancing equity, inclusion, and community-engaged care. Successful candidates will practice at UCR Health clinical sites and/or affiliated hospitals and practices throughout Riverside County, Orange County, and the Coachella Valley (Palm Springs region). Faculty appointments may be in one of several academic series, including: • Professor of Clinical X • Health Sciences Clinical Professor • Adjunct Professor • Professor in Residence Appointments may be made at the Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor rank, commensurate with qualifications and experience. UCR Psychiatry supports a vibrant educational mission, including a medical student education program, an ACGME-accredited psychiatry residency, and fellowships in child and adolescent psychiatry and addiction medicine. The University of California, Riverside is a leading public research university known for its diverse student body and commitment to expanding pathways to higher education for first-generation and historically underrepresented students. Advancement through the faculty ranks at the University of California occurs through structured, merit-based academic review, typically every two to three years, and includes peer evaluation of clinical care, teaching, scholarship, and service. Basic Qualifications • M.D., D.O., or equivalent degree • Eligible for licensure to practice medicine in the State of California by the time of appointment • Board certified or board eligible in Psychiatry by the American Board of Psychiatry and Neurology (board eligibility limited to within three years of completing residency training) Additional Expectations Successful candidates will demonstrate a strong commitment to: • Excellence in clinical care • Education of medical students, residents, and fellows • Scholarly activity and academic development • University, professional, and community service appropriate to the faculty series Candidates must also qualify for medical staff privileges at affiliated clinical sites. In-Res titles are intended to be used for individuals supported by non-State funds. Faculty candidates in Adjunct Professor Series may hold an academic position at another institution. Candidates must possess an M.D. or Ph.D. with research or teaching experience. The posted UC salary scales ( Academic salaries | UCOP ) set the minimum pay determined by rank and step at appointment. See Table 5 for the salary range. The Base Salary range for this position is $131,200 - $344,400. This position includes membership in the health sciences compensation plan. ( 2021 02 11 Hscp%20 Plan ), which provides for eligibility for additional compensation. HS Clinical Professor: Apm 278 Clinical X Professor: Apm 275 In-Residence Professor: Apm 270 Adjunct Professor: Apm 280 TO APPLY: Open Faculty & Academic Positions | School of Medicine Initial review of applications will begin on August 5, 2026 and applicants will be considered until the positions are filled. This posting is for Health Sciences Compensation Plan (HSCP) clinical faculty with clinical care, teaching, and research involvement. If you are interested in a physician position with a primary focus on clinical care only, you may still join our exciting team of physicians by applying through the staff physician posting here: University of California, Riverside - Jobs Qualifications Basic qualifications (required at time of application) Clinical X , Health Sciences, and In-Res Series M.D. or equivalent degree Eligible for licensure in the State of California or have a current California Medical License Board certified or board eligible (only within three years of completing residency) with the American Board of Psychiatry and Neurology Qualify for medical staff privileges at UCR Health and our affiliated hospitals Adjunct Series Possess an M. D. or Ph.D.  with research or teaching experience Preferred qualifications Assistant Rank Excellence in clinical care Experience teaching medical students, residents, and fellows Experience in creative, research, and scholarly activities Assistant, Associate, or Full Rank Additional certification in child & adolescent, geriatric, addiction, forensic and consultation-liaison. Specialty interests in LGBTQ, women’s mental health or reproductive psychiatry, trauma-related disorders, health disparities, health services research, neuropsychiatry, developmental disorders and neurodiversity Experience or interest in telepsychiatry Proficiency in Spanish is desirable. UCR School of Medicine is a minority and Hispanic serving institution. Application Requirements by Level Health Sciences Assistant Clinical Professor Position title: Health Sciences Assistant Clinical Professor Submit a cover letter, most recently updated curriculum vitae, three reference letters, a Statement of Teaching (required), a Statement of Clinical (required), a Statement of Research (optional), and Teaching Evaluations (required). In order to be considered, your application needs to be marked as completed. Document requirements Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae -   Your most recently updated C.V. Statement of Teaching Statement of Clinical Statement of Research (Optional) Teaching Evaluations Reference requirements 3-4 letters of reference required Upload 3 reference letters, or have the system send the request to the letter writers. Apply link: https://aprecruit.ucr.edu/JPF02263 Health Sciences Associate Clinical Professor Position title: Health Sciences Associate Clinical Professor Submit a cover letter, most recently updated curriculum vitae, contact information for five references, a Statement of Teaching (required), a Statement of Clinical (required), a Statement of Research (optional), and Teaching Evaluations (required). In order to be considered, your application needs to be marked 