      "description": "Department of Medicine - Open Rank (JPF02271) - AP Recruit Skip to main content Recruit Home Open Recruitments Department of Medicine - Open Rank (JPF02271) Department of Medicine - Open Rank Apply now to Department of Medicine - Open Rank Job #JPF02271 SOM Internal Medicine / School of Medicine / UC Riverside Position overview Position titles: Health Sciences Clinical Instructor Health Sciences Assistant Clinical Professor Health Sciences Associate Clinical Professor Health Sciences Full Clinical Professor Assistant Professor of Clinical X Associate Professor of Clinical X Professor of Clinical X Application Window Open date: July 17, 2026 Next review date: Tuesday, Sep 15, 2026 at 11:59pm (Pacific Time) Apply by this date to ensure full consideration by the committee. Final date: Wednesday, Jun 30, 2027 at 11:59pm (Pacific Time) Applications will continue to be accepted until this date, but those received after the review date will only be considered if the position has not yet been filled. Position description The Division of Clinical Sciences at the University of California, Riverside is recruiting faculty members in the Department of Medicine. The successful applicant(s) must qualify for an academic appointment in Professor of Clinical X or Health Sciences Clinical Professor series at the Instructor, Assistant, Associate, or Full professor rank. We seek clinical educators to participate in part- time and/or full-time inpatient and outpatient clinical practice in Internal Medicine within an academic setting in one or more of the following clinical specialties: • Cardiology • Dermatology • Endocrinology • Gastroenterology • Geriatrics • Nephrology • Primary Care • Pulmonary • Rheumatology These positions offer excellent opportunities for teaching and pursuing a career in academic medicine with time dedicated to teaching, research, and scholarly activity. Applicants who have completed a clinical fellowship in their respective specialties are preferred. The successful candidate(s) will practice at UC Riverside School of Medicine affiliated Clinics in Inland Southern California. The UCR School of Medicine’s mission is to improve the health of the community in the Inland Empire, one of the most ethnically diverse and medically underserved areas of the country. Basic qualifications M.D. or D.O. degree, or equivalent degree Hold a full and unrestricted license from the Medical Board of California Board Certified by the American Board of Internal Medicine,  or appropriate American Certifying Board or eligible for certification if within 3 years of completing residency. Qualify for medical staff privileges at UCR Health and at UCR affiliated health settings Additional qualifications Demonstrated experience in teaching residents and medical students. Preferred qualifications Commitment to UCR School of Medicine Mission, Vision, Diversity, & Values Statements | School of Medicine Health Sciences Clinical Instructor Rank A successful candidate should complete a high-quality postgraduate clinical training or be accepted into a postgraduate clinical training program. Must be eligible for one of the medical specialty boards and have a clear potential as a clinical teacher. At this rank, the initial appointment is limited to one year. Assistant, Associate and Full Professor Rank Successful candidates will also be expected to participate in research, scholarly activities, University and public service appropriate for the academic appointments in Professor of Clinical X or Health Sciences Clinical series. Rank will be determined based on qualifications and experience. Advancement through the faculty ranks at the University of California is through a series of structured, merit-based evaluations, occurring every 2-3 years, each of which includes substantial peer input. The posted UC salary scales Academic salaries | UCOP set the minimum pay determined by rank and step at appointment. See Table 5 for the salary range. The Salary range for this position is $131,200 - 344,400. This position includes membership in the health sciences compensation plan HSCP Plan , which provides for eligibility for additional compensation. Initial review of applications will begin on August 26, and applicants will be considered until the positions are filled. Health Sciences Clinical Professor: APM 278 Clinical X Professor: APM 275 Initial review of applications will begin on August 30, 2026 and applicants will be considered until the positions are filled. This posting is for Health Sciences Compensation Plan (HSCP) clinical faculty with clinical care, teaching, and research involvement. If you are interested in a physician position with a primary focus on clinical care only, you may still join our exciting team of physicians by applying through the staff physician posting here: University of California, Riverside - Jobs Qualifications Basic qualifications (required at time of application) Possess an M.D. or equivalent degree Has current California Medical License or is eligible for licensure in the State of California. Board Certified or Board Eligible in Internal Medicine or appropriate American Certifying Board. Must qualify for medical staff privileges at UCR Health and our affiliated hospitals. Experience in clinical practice providing inpatient and outpatient care in Internal Medicine. Preferred qualifications Assistant Rank Experience in scholarly activities. Completed clinical fellowship in the respective specialties. Assistant, Associate, or Full Rank UCR is a world-class research university with an exceptionally diverse undergraduate student body. Its mission is explicitly linked to providing routes to educational success for underrepresented and first-generation college students. A commitment to this mission is a preferred qualification. Application Requirements by Level Health Sciences Clinical Instructor Position title: Health Sciences Clinical Instructor Submit a cover letter, most recently updated curriculum vitae, three reference letters, a Statement of Research, and a Contribution to Diversity Statement. In order to be considered, your application needs to be marked as completed. Document requirements Curriculum Vitae -   Your most recently updated C.V. Cover Letter Statement of Research (Optional) Statement of Teaching (Optional) Reference requirements 3-4 letters of reference required Upload 3 reference letters, or have the system send the request to the letter writers. Apply link: https://aprecruit.ucr.edu/JPF02271 Health Sciences Assistant Clinical Professor Position title: Health Sciences Assistant Clinical Professor Submit a cover letter, most recently updated curriculum vitae, three reference letters, a Statement of Teaching (required), a Statement of Research (optional), and Teaching Evaluations (required). In order to be considered, your application needs to be marked as completed. Document requirements Curriculum Vitae -   Your most recently updated C.V. Cover Letter Statement of Research (Optional) Statement of Teaching Teaching Evaluation Reference requirements 3-4 letters of reference required Upload 3 reference letters, or have the system send the request to the letter writers. Apply link: https://aprecruit.ucr.edu/JPF02271 Health Sciences Associate Clinical Professor Position title: Health Sciences Associate Clinical Professor Submit a cover letter, most recently updated curriculum vitae, contact information for five references, a Statement of Teaching (required), a Statement of Research (optional), and Teaching Evaluations (required). In order to be considered, your application needs to be marked as completed. Document requirements Curriculum Vitae -   Your most recently updated C.V. Cover Letter Statement of Research (Optional) Statement of Teaching Teaching Evaluation Reference requirements 5-7 required (contact information only) Provide contact information for 5-7 referees. Apply link: https://aprecruit.ucr.edu/JPF02271 Health Sciences Full Clinical Professor Position title: Health Sciences Full Clinical Professor Submit a cover letter, most recently updated curriculum vitae, contact information for six to eight references, a Statement of Teaching, a Statement of Research, Teaching Evaluations and a Contribution to Diversity Statement. In order to be considered, your application needs to be marked as completed. Document requirements Curriculum Vitae -   Your most recently updated C.V. Cover Letter Statement of Research (Optional) Statement of Teaching Teaching Evaluation Reference requirements 5-7 required (contact information only) Provide contact information for 5-7 referees. Apply link: https://aprecruit.ucr.edu/JPF02271 Assistant Professor of Clinical X Position title: Assistant Professor of Clinical X Submit a cover letter, most recently updated curriculum vitae, six reference letters, a Statement of Teaching (required), a Statement of Research (optional), and Teaching Evaluations (required). In order to be considered, your application needs to be marked as completed. Document requirements Curriculum Vitae -   Your most recently updated C.V. Cover Letter Statement of Research (Optional) Statement of Teaching Teaching Evaluation Reference requirements 6-7 letters of reference required Upload 6 reference letters, or have the system send the request to the letter writers. Apply link: https://aprecruit.ucr.edu/JPF02271 Associate Professor of Clinical X Position title: Associate Professor of Clinical X Submit a cover letter, most recently updated curriculum vitae, contact information for six references, a Statement of Teaching (required), a Statement of Research (optional), and Teaching Evaluations (required). In order to be considered, your application needs to be marked as completed. Document requirements Curriculum Vitae -   Your most recently updated C.V. Cover Letter Statement of Research (Optional) Statement of Teaching Teaching Evaluation Reference requirements 6-9 required (contac