or full-time inpatient and outpatient clinical practice in General Obstetrics and Gynecology, and Gynecologic Oncology. These positions offer excellent opportunities for teaching and pursuing a career in academic medicine with time dedicated to teaching and scholarly activity. The successful candidates will practice at UC Riverside School of Medicine affiliated hospitals in Riverside and surrounding areas. The successful candidate must qualify for an academic appointment in Professor of Clinical X or Health Sciences Clinical Professor series at the Instructor, Assistant, Associate, or Full professor rank. Academic rank will be determined based on qualifications and experience with advancement through a series of structured, merit-based evaluations, occurring every 2-3 years, each of which includes substantial peer input. Basic qualifications M.D. or D.O. degree, or equivalent degree Hold a full and unrestricted license from the Medical Board of California Board Certified by the American Board of Obstetrics and Gynecology or eligible for certification if within 3 years of completing residency. Qualify for medical staff privileges at UCR Health and at UCR affiliated health settings Additional qualifications Demonstrated experience in teaching residents and medical students Preferred qualifications Commitment to UCR School of Medicine Mission, Vision, Diversity, & Values Statements | School of Medicine Health Sciences Clinical Instructor Rank A successful candidate should complete a high-quality postgraduate clinical training or be accepted into a postgraduate clinical training program. Must be eligible for one of the medical specialty boards and have a clear potential as a clinical teacher. At this rank, the initial appointment is limited to one year. Assistant, Associate and Full Professor Rank: Successful candidates will also be expected to participate in research, scholarly activities, University and public service appropriate for the academic appointments in Profe