    "https://aprecruit.ucr.edu/JPF02317": {
      "title": "Division of Undergraduate Education Teaching Assistant (2026-2027) (JPF02317)",
      "description": "Division of Undergraduate Education Teaching Assistant (2026-2027) (JPF02317) - AP Recruit Skip to main content Recruit Home Open Recruitments Division of Undergraduate Education Teaching Assistant (2026-2027) (JPF02317) Division of Undergraduate Education Teaching Assistant (2026-2027) Apply now to Division of Undergraduate Education Teaching Assistant (2026-2027) Job #JPF02317 Undergraduate Education / Undergraduate Education / UC Riverside Position overview Position title: Teaching Assistant; Teaching Fellow Salary range: $4,100.00 to $4,370.00 per month Table 18 Anticipated start: September 21, 2026 Application Window Open date: July 27, 2026 Most recent review date: Monday, Aug 10, 2026 at 11:59pm (Pacific Time) Applications received after this date will be reviewed by the search committee if the position has not yet been filled. Final date: Wednesday, Jun 30, 2027 at 11:59pm (Pacific Time) Applications will continue to be accepted until this date, but those received after the review date will only be considered if the position has not yet been filled. Position description The Division of Undergraduate Education (DUE) at the University of California, Riverside is accepting applications for Teaching Assistant (T.A.) position for the 2026-2027 academic year. Anticipated start date: September 21, 2026 Salary: See UCOP salary table 18 for current starting salary: (Salary Scale Table 18 Webpage) Teaching Assistant appointments will not exceed 50% Job Description: Division of Undergraduate Education T.A. is assigned academic responsibilities and is supervised by the faculty in charge and R’Course Program Coordinator. This role involves instruction of one to two class meetings per week of UGRC 001A and UGRC 001B while actively supporting student success through individual and small-group mentorship and timely feedback on coursework. In addition to instruction, the position drives curriculum development by designing lesson materials for the UGRC 001ABC series and fosters peer educator growth by observing R’Course Student Facilitators and providing structured, actionable feedback. Beyond teaching and mentorship, the role also ensures smooth operational workflows by assisting with general program administration. TA-ships are full academic year appointments at 50% FTE. Candidates must be available to serve as T.A. for the entire academic year (09/21/2026 – 06/15/2027). Basic Qualifications: (Must meet all listed qualifications) • Bachelor's degree • Must be a registered UC Riverside graduate student in full-time residence (registered for 12 units per term) • Maintenance of a qualifying grade point average • Must be academically eligible to hold the appointment per UC Riverside Graduate Policy Webpage Preferred Qualifications: Candidates should have experience in higher education, especially in instructional design and teacher development. Prior teaching experience may be considered but is not required. The University of California, Riverside is a world-class research university with an exceptionally diverse undergraduate student body. UCR is a member institution of the American Association of Universities (AAU) and the Alliance of Hispanic Serving Research Universities (HSRU). A commitment to the UCR mission UCR Mission Statement Webpage is a preferred qualification. Application Instructions: Application materials will be submitted using UCR's online application system located at UCRecruit.edu . Complete applications will include a current C.V, Cover Letter, teaching evaluations (if available), a letter from their Department Chair or Graduate Advisor verifying eligibility and availability for the year, and at least one letter of recommendation. To ensure full consideration, application materials should be received by Friday, July 31, 2026. Qualified applicants will be asked to evaluate and comment on a sample student syllabus and may be invited to interview. The University of California Teaching Assistants are represented by the UAW-AFL-CIO BX Bargaining Contact Webpage . Qualifications Basic qualifications (required at time of application) • Bachelor's degree • Must be a registered UC Riverside graduate student in full-time residence (registered for 12 units per term ) • Maintenance of a qualifying grade point average • Academically eligible to hold the appointment (per UC Riverside Graduate Policy Webpage) Preferred qualifications Candidates must be excellent writers. Prior teaching experience may be considered but is not required. The University of California, Riverside is a world-class research university with an exceptionally diverse undergraduate student body. UCR is a member institution of the American Association of Universities (AAU) and the Alliance of Hispanic Serving Research Universities (HSRU). A commitment to the UCR mission [ UCR Mission Statement Webpage ] is a preferred qualification. Application Requirements Document requirements Curriculum Vitae -   Your most recently updated C.V. Cover Letter Teaching Evaluations (Optional) Eligibility / Availability verification -   Please provide letter(s) from your Department Chair and/or Graduate Advisor verifying your eligibility and availability for the 2026-2027 Academic Year [ Academic Calendar ]. Statement of Teaching (Optional) Reference requirements 1-2 letters of reference required Applicants will be asked to name references, and the applicant must request a letter to complete their application. Apply link: https://aprecruit.ucr.edu/JPF02317 Help contact: ericc@ucr.edu About UC Riverside The University of California, Riverside is a world-class research university with an exceptionally diverse undergraduate student body. UCR is a member institution of the American Association of Universities (AAU) and the Alliance of Hispanic Serving Research Universities (HSRU).  A commitment to the UCR mission ( https://apro.ucr.edu/mission-statement ) is a preferred qualification. We seek to hire scholars who will both a