    "https://aprecruit.ucr.edu/JPF02339": {
      "title": "Professional Researcher Series",
      "description": "Professional Researcher Series in Biomedical Sciences (JPF02339) - AP Recruit Skip to main content Recruit Home Open Recruitments Professional Researcher Series in Biomedical Sciences (JPF02339) Professional Researcher Series in Biomedical Sciences Apply now to Professional Researcher Series in Biomedical Sciences Job #JPF02339 Biomedical Sciences / School of Medicine / UC Riverside Position overview Position titles: Assistant Professional Researcher Associate Professional Researcher Professional Researcher Salary range: The posted UC salary scales UCOP compensation index set the minimum pay determined by rank and step at appointment. \n\nSee Table 13B for the Professional Researcher Salary range, the base salary range for this series $96,700 - $257,100. See Table 13B-N for the non-exempt salary range, the base salary range for non-exempt Professional Researchers is $46.32 - $123.14. Application Window Open date: August 13, 2026 Most recent review date: Thursday, Aug 27, 2026 at 11:59pm (Pacific Time) Applications received after this date will be reviewed by the search committee if the position has not yet been filled. Final date: Wednesday, Jun 30, 2027 at 11:59pm (Pacific Time) Applications will continue to be accepted until this date, but those received after the review date will only be considered if the position has not yet been filled. Position description Professional Researcher Series positions are occasionally available throughout the year in the Division of Biomedical Sciences in the School of Medicine at the University of California, Riverside. The Division is conducting an open search for Professional Researchers in various disciplines. Positions are filled as they become available based on the funds and priorities of different laboratories or research centers. Initial appointment for the Professional Researcher Series is for one year, and renewal is based on availability of support. Successful candidates must also have clear potential or demonstrated ability to work effectively with a diverse student body. Salary commensurate with experience. The posted UC salary scales UCOP compensation index set the minimum pay determined by rank and step at appointment. Advancement through the ranks at the University of California is through a series of structured, merit-based evaluations, occurring every 2-3 years, each of which includes substantial peer input. Professional Researcher Series These positions are academic appointments in the non-senate series and do not have teaching responsibilities. Candidates must demonstrate continuous and effective engagement in independent and creative research activity of high quality and significance, equivalent to the Professor series. Assistant Professional Researchers must possess a Ph.D. degree (or its equivalent). Associate and Full Professional Researchers must possess a Ph.D. degree (or its equivalent) and demonstrate University and/or public service. See Table 13B for the Professional Researcher Salary range, the base salary range for this series is $96,700 - $257,100. See Table 13B-N for the non-exempt salary range, the base salary range for non-exempt Professional Researchers is $46.32 - $123.14. Founded in 2013, the School of Medicine at UCR is the sixth University of California Medical School and serves the rapidly growing Inland Southern California region by training a much-needed physician workforce and catalyzing innovations in research, education, and healthcare delivery. The UCR School of Medicine’s mission is to improve the health of the community in the Inland Empire, one of the most ethnically diverse and medically underserved areas of the country. Qualifications Basic qualifications (required at time of application) Assistant Professional Researcher rank Must possess a Ph.D. degree (or equivalent degree) and experience in the relevant field. Must possess research qualifications and accomplishments equivalent to those for the Professor series, including demonstrated continuous and effective engagement in independent and creative activity of high quality and significance. Professional competence and activity equivalent to those for the Professor series. Associate and Full Professional Researcher ranks Must possess a Ph.D. degree (or equivalent degree) and experience in the relevant field. Must possess research qualifications and accomplishments equivalent to those for the Professor series, including demonstrated continuous and effective engagement in independent and creative activity of high quality and significance. Professional competence and activity equivalent to those for the Professor series. University and/or public service. Preferred qualifications Hold a strong record of specialized training and experience in grant writing. UCR is a world-class research university with an exceptionally diverse undergraduate student body. Its mission is explicitly linked to providing routes to educational success for underrepresented and first-generation college students. A commitment to this mission is a preferred qualification. Application Requirements by Level Assistant Professional Researcher Position title: Assistant Professional Researcher Submit a most recently updated curriculum vitae and contact information for three to five references. To be considered, your application needs to be marked as completed. Document requirements Curriculum Vitae -   Your most recently updated C.V. Cover Letter (Optional) Statement of Research (Optional) Reference requirements 3-5 required (contact information only) Provide contact information for 3-5 referees. Apply link: https://aprecruit.ucr.edu/JPF02339 Associate Professional Researcher Position title: Associate Professional Researcher Submit a most recently updated curriculum vitae and contact information for six to seven references. To be considered, your application needs to be marked as completed. Document requirements Curriculum Vitae -   Your most recently updated C.V. 